 encounter by the enraged Rāvana, resembling a venomous serpent, dived into the dauntless and heroic Laks maņa; and (the dart) exceedingly splendid and blazing, possessed of dreadful impetuosity and resembling the tongue of the king of serpents, smote Lakşmaņa in his mighty chest. And with his breast riven by the dart driving deep through the force of Rāvana, Lakşmaņa fell down to the earth.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088034","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d5c6af0b1d1af7886ac56c7c6e6da5709ac2b55363e808a938456be91a9f225b","compact":"4c032f16666591eca8b9a7690f59c26bfbaf420b6bb2b7e1d3cbf25a5510218a","nasal":"4c032f16666591eca8b9a7690f59c26bfbaf420b6bb2b7e1d3cbf25a5510218a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-35","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":35,"english":"But the dart discharged in the encounter by the enraged Rāvana, resembling a venomous serpent, dived into the dauntless and heroic Laks maņa; and (the dart) exceedingly splendid and blazing, possessed of dreadful impetuosity and resembling the tongue of the king of serpents, smote Lakşmaņa in his mighty chest. And with his breast riven by the dart driving deep through the force of Rāvana, Lakşmaņa fell down to the earth.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.796,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088035","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7eb6ef04775e581d516cd3b5a420efb6097143783f4a8a31efe57abf2c11a73f","compact":"01480271518d937e7577f29c2157b5e7dc6e9484d3569c9f2dd1e7cdf099ccdc","nasal":"760b165bf9fb13c5f4cd46acbfd0647b897a2d23a367aee5489cdf9c0aa41b26"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-36","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":36,"english":"Rāghava, standing by seeing Lakşmaņa in that plight, had his heart overspread with sorrow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088036","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d0a09e04198be6491001db713640d8ab0b14e0efaeb0cb3db6a216edf18d1b86","compact":"6c2d1d00df96c4109f518811a9948f6740334fa5d320ab87f5124120f8dfce14","nasal":"5cb6cb2939c21c5f62f48ee7eb69533e17d9b5213b88ba9696518275d95b6f7f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-37","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":37,"english":"But reflecting only for a while, he with his eyes surcharged with tears was filled with greater martial ardour, and resembled the fire risen at the universal dissolution. Then thinking.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.434,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088037","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a04062a0a8c6c7a532c49efd543092dd99e57ce35f6c08c7f8e2506babd23edc","compact":"a9dabc2a1ab760f8e175a417de40b9bdd9678abfbb8f6707bcfea5adfc10352b","nasal":"f313ebad4a94faee4c697997131d1293bd8b1d09bd42d15ea7be2373bd6d1348"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-38","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":38,"english":"This is not the time to indulge in grief he, gazing at Lakşmaņa, entered into a terrific encounter resolved upon slaying Rāvaņa, laying under contribution his dearest energies.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088038","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bb1ba089e4c6201ab0c3b43509d8d7bde4db639e5e4f42d60685529b38f05e69","compact":"b33320a3010bf0b3b81be52fcb963e6ba8393ed05c25e425547b3a7622c79dca","nasal":"ab48e72b4343752ec94dc312ea98fe9ccd06035eee74abf77641262b9016dc8b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-39","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":39,"english":"Rāma saw Lakşmaņa with his chest riven by the dart in the mighty conflict lying drenched in blood, and resembling a hill with serpents present in it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088039","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fc30ac3a1eb85a58fc5fea0428153fbd85c1c95c929fbc54a16d43eeb11b5fd0","compact":"50b78d596102a807e24ba6316701bb3a67f296de778d053e4a7083da31e25d13","nasal":"ebcc1f715bd1c02a8d8791b2c4e8b69b957f3a413f51fde89a49aa50c179ecb9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-40","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":40,"english":"In spite of all their efforts, the foremost monkeys failed to extract the dart which had been hurled by the powerful Rāvaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.612,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088040","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a3b21337b83c855dee1206fb67a530b540573412acb1d528176e6052492d0027","compact":"21bdb5fc82623bf69e18f59790bf63c2d2e0c715c8f5038b6a2b4ed24d56c554","nasal":"21bdb5fc82623bf69e18f59790bf63c2d2e0c715c8f5038b6a2b4ed24d56c554"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-41","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":41,"english":"In the encounter the mighty Rāma grasping the dreadful dart with his hands, extracted the same the wrathfully snapped it* *The commentator has a characteristic note. This dart, having pierced the foe, used always to return to Ravana. But Rama, whose was the Lord himself, having spoken to it as he did, it could not this time go back; and Rāma snapped it, which none else could do.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.525,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088041","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6c85765a99f9f4e750e79ee7ad3dd7e20b76b3cce1288e15b42b99c6d67d2ffd","compact":"b97cfc3c7d1b453deda9993952abf90fc672307dc34290e19cf946afd0c046e2","nasal":"0164955d3c41165bb8d7cefc9fdfd8b326f0189f750a596bcf0e6a7ecec0ee11"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-42","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":42,"english":"As he (Rāma) was engaged in pulling the dart out, the mighty Ravana kept pouring marrowpiercing shafts all over his person.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088042","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"09a6a670311d6b840b10069dad3d4e80c765f49233d95c43629d7b1bd67f0ca3","compact":"954877476c83ab2b5fb05918a74fa2a93ed3b2bf0b56c645daa7b7d9ff0ccf17","nasal":"954877476c83ab2b5fb05918a74fa2a93ed3b2bf0b56c645daa7b7d9ff0ccf17"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-43","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":43,"english":"Thinking nothing of those arrows. Rāma embracing Lakşmaņa, spoke to Hanuman and the mighty monkey, Sugriva.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088043","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aaf622e38d282fa2a451a947b00651413c9317cd2fef24ca9f04c0007609b77c","compact":"25e1f83780a9bd56721ccdc2737b078f49ae809b07c8509d52e5130f820d5bbd","nasal":"73cb63410ef1894b7db9bcc7861abf7beb2794e025a12a0860295c8825bfe49a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-44","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":44,"english":"You foremost of monkeys do you stay here surrounding Lakṣmaṇa. The opportunity for putting forth my prowess which I had sought, is present. I shall slay this wicked minded Ten-necked one, who is resolved to pursue the course of unrighteousness. Even as on the expire of summer the Cătaka is eager for the sight of clouds, I had long been eager to obtain a sight of (Ravana).","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.387,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-37","DUTT-6-100-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088044","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d2c179a96fa44867f54f4009e58d768f14ebd40cbd502c92d42387fa44088101","compact":"7dfb439849107de8f73d8019170ad371cd08434f225396258554db348dd9f848","nasal":"9b228ffa550006c16ba406d573596ecae42a1a3cd69dfe5d4086705da1f9bc3e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-45","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":45,"english":"You monkeys, this I swear to you-this very hour not long after you will see this world without Rāvaņa or Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.891,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088045","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8c4b2fd338a4219ec70fa046da2b17602a6d03a68ee020ed37bbc98fdc69a40a","compact":"42a5873e9cdb9ba49b9fc8a97cbf54fa07b75990df86b1895b035ca08c1b254e","nasal":"42a5873e9cdb9ba49b9fc8a97cbf54fa07b75990df86b1895b035ca08c1b254e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-46","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":46,"english":"To-day having slain Rāvaņa in battle, I shall renounce all sorrow arising from the loss of my kingdom, from my sojourn in the woods, from my wandering in Daņdaka, from the ravishment of Vaidehi, from encounter with the Raksasa, all the terrible evils that I have suffered and all the troubles resembling hell.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088046","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"04474b5c1e3f1baff94e639a84b58e895f8ebb86389aebb2e0fe7e21bf731387","compact":"08166e378a5dc5ab6fb696c6ec3724c7b92d5cecd8018cd3cc919022336aea20","nasal":"f0d97f4fbf8e724e238ee0c3db2ba5f73da0d45e3c8e3003c5144b50ee7a70a7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-47","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":47,"english":"To-day having slain Rāvaņa in battle, I shall renounce all sorrow arising from the loss of my kingdom, from my sojourn in the woods, from my wandering in Daņdaka, from the ravishment of Vaidehi, from encounter with the Raksasa, all the terrible evils that I have suffered and all the troubles resembling hell.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.385,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088047","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e77e58080f8431d0b538d17915a9c5d7392e343cab24222e26ae49ee8765e038","compact":"d57f9e254d3560c00536f79c86c42586b053fb44dac3071bef0b8bb3f5843332","nasal":"d57f9e254d3560c00536f79c86c42586b053fb44dac3071bef0b8bb3f5843332"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-48","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":48,"english":"He for whom I have brought over the monkey-forces, made Sugriva king, slaying Vali in battle, for whom I have crossed the ocean and constructed a bridge over the deep-the same has been come at by me in conflict, and the same has come within the range of my vision.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088048","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"853189691a1b367626a498b07c5086629bb98bad64f6774e3a0c3cdc608b8485","compact":"ce7708f8fb9632b9504eeb8b5b3d1b6b0fb1ddbec368e169c3e1f71c3652e9e5","nasal":"ce7708f8fb9