uddha","sarga":88,"verse":51,"english":"Do you, you irrepressible ones, you foremost of monkeys, seated at the brow of the mountain, behold the battle between me and Rāvaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-43"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088051","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fa0114b6d8f4338139d86a1cab081167162c5633317c755410caca4384f09edb","compact":"13f228cfc4ddec74fa2f06bfb1ddbf795e2ccc7a049335739d44d086b4724611","nasal":"13f228cfc4ddec74fa2f06bfb1ddbf795e2ccc7a049335739d44d086b4724611"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-52","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":52,"english":"Today let the three worlds with the Gandharvas, and the Siddhas, and the Caranas, see that for which Rāma is Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.46,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-44"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088052","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"51513080a6d0fc427eb34b7f4b7caf7417b29a63e052d1efca9ea42c162d7aeb","compact":"ad056273ff00f863b15bf43a37e48879ba2a96692d2d5f64a94b802a7847f6f6","nasal":"2dbc5ef49c9d2f375bf58851c11d120c1b81949613486e1c3e61d1d3e8d80018"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-88-53","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":88,"verse":53,"english":"Today I shall do a deed of which the worlds with the mobile and the immobile and the gods, shall speak as long as the Earth sustain (creatures.)","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-100-45"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6088053","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"addebea51983dcf7e9c252fe66fe58c09b87bbecf542fe7e804f78ab701a3569","compact":"a1fab1be7d13ec281e98fe44e8b1e097cda90e94132454223940bb3921a36132","nasal":"7d74